/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (When vertical earth pressure from a load occurs on the top of a corrugated steel plate structure, the lateral earth pressure resists it. At this point, the vertical and lateral earth pressures form a stable and uniform load distribution. This type of load distribution \(hoop compression effect\) suppresses the bending moment and has the structural characteristic of being subject to compressive forces.)
/E (When vertical earth pressure from a load occurs on the top of a corrugated steel plate structure, the lateral earth pressure resists it. At this point, the vertical and lateral earth pressures form a stable and uniform load distribution. This type of load distribution \(hoop compression effect\) suppresses the bending moment and has the structural characteristic of being subject to compressive forces.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [27]
>>
